# Complete GitHub Upload & Local Setup Guide

This guide will help you upload the MedBot Enhanced project to GitHub and run it locally.

## 📋 Prerequisites

- Git installed: https://git-scm.com/download
- GitHub account: https://github.com
- Python 3.8+
- Docker (optional, for containerized deployment)

---

## 🚀 Step 1: Initialize Git Repository

### On Your Local Machine

```bash
# Navigate to project directory
cd medbot-enhanced

# Initialize git repository
git init

# Configure git (replace with your details)
git config user.name "Your Name"
git config user.email "your.email@example.com"

# Optional: Set these globally (add --global flag)
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your.email@example.com"
```

---

## 🌐 Step 2: Create GitHub Repository

### Via GitHub Web Interface

1. **Go to GitHub.com**
   - Log in to your GitHub account
   - Click the "+" icon in top-right corner
   - Select "New repository"

2. **Configure Repository**
   - Repository name: `medbot-enhanced`
   - Description: "Healthcare FAQ Chatbot with Full Automation"
   - Choose "Public" or "Private"
   - ❌ DO NOT initialize with README, .gitignore, or license (we have our own)
   - Click "Create repository"

3. **Copy Repository URL**
   - Copy the HTTPS or SSH URL shown after creation
   - Example: `https://github.com/your-username/medbot-enhanced.git`

---

## 📤 Step 3: Add All Files to Git

```bash
# Add all files to staging area
git add .

# View what will be committed
git status

# Should show files ready to commit (green color)
```

---

## ✅ Step 4: First Commit

```bash
# Create initial commit
git commit -m "Initial commit: MedBot Enhanced - Healthcare chatbot with automation"

# View commit history
git log --oneline
```

---

## 🔗 Step 5: Connect to GitHub Repository

```bash
# Add GitHub repository as remote
# Replace URL with your repository URL
git remote add origin https://github.com/your-username/medbot-enhanced.git

# Verify remote was added
git remote -v

# Should show:
# origin  https://github.com/your-username/medbot-enhanced.git (fetch)
# origin  https://github.com/your-username/medbot-enhanced.git (push)
```

---

## 🚀 Step 6: Push to GitHub

```bash
# Rename branch to main (GitHub default)
git branch -M main

# Push to GitHub
git push -u origin main

# First push will ask for credentials
# Enter your GitHub username and password/token
```

### Using GitHub Token (Recommended)

1. **Create Personal Access Token**
   - Go to GitHub Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens
   - Click "Generate new token"
   - Select scopes: `repo`, `gist`
   - Click "Generate token"
   - Copy the token

2. **Use Token for Authentication**
   ```bash
   git push -u origin main
   # Username: your-github-username
   # Password: paste-your-token-here
   ```

---

## ✨ Step 7: Verify on GitHub

1. **Go to your repository**
   - Visit: `https://github.com/your-username/medbot-enhanced`
   - All files should be visible

2. **Check Project Structure**
   - Verify all files were uploaded
   - README.md should display on main page
   - Click through folders to confirm structure

---

## 🔄 Step 8: Cloning for Local Development

To clone on another machine:

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/your-username/medbot-enhanced.git
cd medbot-enhanced

# Setup and run (see below)
```

