## 🐛 Troubleshooting

### Issue: "Repository already exists"

```bash
# Solution: Remove .git folder and reinitialize
rm -rf .git
git init
```

### Issue: "Permission denied" when pushing

```bash
# Use SSH instead (if configured):
git remote set-url origin git@github.com:username/repo.git

# Or authenticate with token (see Step 6)
```

### Issue: "fatal: 'origin' does not appear to be a 'git' repository"

```bash
# Add remote again
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repo.git
```

### Issue: Files not appearing on GitHub

```bash
# Ensure .gitignore is not blocking files
# Check file status
git status

# Force add if needed
git add -f filename

# Commit and push
git commit -m "Force add file"
git push origin main
```

